IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `dog-act-domain`

-- =============================================================================
-- Dog Act 1976 (Western Australia) -- Protection of stock/vermin; nuisance dogs
--
-- Isomorphic encoding of Part VI Division 3 ("Protection of stock; vermin
-- disease and parasite control", ss 34-35) and Division 4 ("Control of
-- nuisance", s 38), as at the compilation dated 28 Nov 2024
-- [version 08-b0-00], re-verified current 2026-09-09. Sections 36 and 37
-- were REPEALED before this compilation (36: No. 18 of 2013 s. 45; 37:
-- No. 23 of 1987 s. 30) and do not exist as live provisions -- their
-- absence from this file is not an omission, it mirrors the Act itself.
--
-- Source: lines 1234-1270 of mrdoc_47983.txt (verbatim WA Dog Act 1976
-- compilation). The shared s. 3 building blocks this file reads
-- (DogProfile, `the dog is a dangerous dog`, the Penalty record shape)
-- live in dog-act-domain.l4, imported above.
--
-- SCOPED OUT (cited at their site with @ref, never expanded): s. 27
-- (approved kennel establishment licensing -- s 38(6)'s exemption gate).
-- "Prescribed" matters (form, noise level/method/period/count under
-- s 38(1)(c), the poison-related Act referred to in s 34(4)(b)) are left
-- as fact-supplied booleans without a specific section citation, since the
-- text names no particular section for them (regulations generally, or an
-- unspecified other Act).
-- =============================================================================

§ `Part VI, Division 3 -- Protection of stock; vermin disease and parasite control`
§§ `34. Protection of livestock`

-- s 34(1) -- lawful killing of a dog caught attacking an animal or bird.
DECLARE `S34(1) Facts` HAS
    `person owns, or is for the time being lawfully in charge of, the animal or bird` IS A BOOLEAN
    `person found a dog attacking that animal or bird`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is no other way of stopping the attack`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice was given to a police officer as soon as is practicable after the shooting or destruction` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(1)
GIVEN f IS A `S34(1) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`shooting or destroying a dog under s 34(1) is lawful` f MEANS
        f's `person owns, or is for the time being lawfully in charge of, the animal or bird`
    AND f's `person found a dog attacking that animal or bird`
    AND f's `there is no other way of stopping the attack`
    AND f's `notice was given to a police officer as soon as is practicable after the shooting or destruction`

-- s 34(2) -- lawful killing of an unaccompanied dog found among confined
-- livestock. "Livestock" is defined, for the whole of s. 34, as horse,
-- cattle, sheep, swine, goats or poultry confined in the enclosed place.
-- Whether the dog's own owner is known or not is stated to be immaterial,
-- so no field carries that fact.
DECLARE `S34(2) Facts` HAS
    `person is the owner or occupier of the enclosed paddock, field, yard or other place confining the livestock, or is acting under that owner's or occupier's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog was found within that enclosed place`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dog was not accompanied by some person`    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(2)
GIVEN f IS A `S34(2) Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`shooting or destroying a dog under s 34(2) is lawful` f MEANS
        f's `person is the owner or occupier of the enclosed paddock, field, yard or other place confining the livestock, or is acting under that owner's or occupier's authority`
    AND f's `the dog was found within that enclosed place`
    AND f's `the dog was not accompanied by some person`

-- s 34(3) -- an evidentiary provision, not a duty or offence: in a civil or
-- penal proceeding arising from an attack on an animal or bird, or the
-- worrying or chasing of livestock, the stated fact is PRIMA FACIE (i.e.
-- rebuttable) evidence that the person had the dog in possession or under
-- control for the purposes of the s. 3 "person liable for the control of
-- the dog" definition (imported as `LiableParty` / `the party is a person
-- liable for the control of the dog` from dog-act-domain). s 34(3) does not
-- itself redefine or override that s. 3 test -- it only supplies one way of
-- proving the "has the dog in possession or under control" disjunct of it
-- -- so this predicate is encoded standalone rather than by constructing a
-- LiableParty value.
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(3)
GIVEN `the dog was, immediately before the attack or the worrying or chasing, in company with, or had been seen continuously and closely following, a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(3) prima facie evidence that the person had the dog in possession or under control` `the dog was, immediately before the attack or the worrying or chasing, in company with, or had been seen continuously and closely following, a person` MEANS
    `the dog was, immediately before the attack or the worrying or chasing, in company with, or had been seen continuously and closely following, a person`

-- s 34(4) -- lawful poison-baiting for the protection of livestock, and the
-- offence that arises when the conditions are not met.
DECLARE PoisonLayingFacts HAS
    `laying of the poison was reasonably necessary for the protection of livestock confined or depasturing on the land`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `poison is not laid within 20 m of any road, reserve or public place`                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `laying of the poison is authorised in the material circumstances by or under an Act relating to the prevention, destruction or eradication of specific kinds of animal or of animals in specified circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
        -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(4)(b) -- the authorising Act is not named in this section; scoped out, fact-supplied
    `poison is not laid so as to endanger children or indigenous birds or animals`                                                                        IS A BOOLEAN

-- AMBIGUITY (F-S34-POISON-OFFENCE-ACTOR): the chapeau introduces the
-- permission for "the owner or occupier of that land or a person acting
-- under his authority", but the offence sentence at the end of s 34(4)
-- says only "a person who lays poison in baits commits an offence",
-- without repeating that narrower actor class. Reading (a): the offence is
-- confined to the same owner/occupier/authorised-person class described in
-- the chapeau, whose poison-laying falls outside the lawful conditions.
-- Reading (b): the offence reaches ANY person who lays poison in baits
-- that is not reasonably necessary for livestock protection and/or does
-- not comply with (a)-(c), regardless of any connection to the land.
-- TAKEN: reading (b) -- the offence sentence introduces its own indefinite
-- "a person" rather than cross-referring to the chapeau's defined actor,
-- and the necessity/compliance test is actor-neutral on its face. This is
-- also the encoding actually adopted below: `PoisonLayingFacts` carries no
-- "is the owner/occupier" field, so the offence predicate is available to
-- any layer of poison. Recorded as F-S34-POISON-OFFENCE-ACTOR in this
-- module's own ambiguities register (this file has no separate
-- sources/fork-register.json entry -- that JSON file's "subject" is
-- dog-act-1976 and its five entries all belong to dog-act-1976.l4).
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(4)
GIVEN f IS A PoisonLayingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`laying poison under s 34(4) is lawful` f MEANS
        f's `laying of the poison was reasonably necessary for the protection of livestock confined or depasturing on the land`
    AND f's `poison is not laid within 20 m of any road, reserve or public place`
    AND f's `laying of the poison is authorised in the material circumstances by or under an Act relating to the prevention, destruction or eradication of specific kinds of animal or of animals in specified circumstances`
    AND f's `poison is not laid so as to endanger children or indigenous birds or animals`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(4)
GIVEN f IS A PoisonLayingFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34(4) offence -- laying poison in baits outside the lawful conditions` f MEANS
    NOT (`laying poison under s 34(4) is lawful` f)

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 34(4) Penalty
`s 34(4) penalty` MEANS
    Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 1_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

§§ `35. Destruction of vermin etc.`

-- An immunity from civil or penal liability, not an offence or a duty: a
-- person taking lawful, reasonable, good-faith measures to destroy vermin
-- or dogs wandering at large is not liable for a wandering dog's resulting
-- death, injury or harm.
DECLARE `S35 Facts` HAS
    `person reasonably and in good faith lawfully took measures for the purpose of destroying vermin or dogs wandering at large` IS A BOOLEAN
    `measures were taken in conformity with the provisions of an Act or the regulations made under it`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a dog wandering at large suffered death, injury or harm as a consequence of those measures`                                 IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 35
GIVEN f IS A `S35 Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`immunity from liability applies under s 35` f MEANS
        f's `person reasonably and in good faith lawfully took measures for the purpose of destroying vermin or dogs wandering at large`
    AND f's `measures were taken in conformity with the provisions of an Act or the regulations made under it`
    AND f's `a dog wandering at large suffered death, injury or harm as a consequence of those measures`

§§ `36-37. [Deleted]`
-- s. 36 was deleted by No. 18 of 2013 s. 45; s. 37 was deleted by
-- No. 23 of 1987 s. 30. Neither the compilation nor this line range carries
-- any former text for them (they appear only as bracketed deletion
-- markers in the source). No operative content to encode -- this heading
-- exists solely so the corpus's section numbering has no silent gap.

§ `Part VI, Division 4 -- Control of nuisance`
§§ `38. Nuisance dogs`

-- s 38(1) -- what makes a dog a "nuisance" for the purposes of this
-- section. Three independent, disjunctive grounds; (c)(i)/(ii) are
-- themselves alternatives within the noise-based ground. The specific
-- noise level/method/period and occurrence-count/period are left as
-- fact-supplied booleans -- the section names no particular section of
-- regulations that prescribes them.
DECLARE NuisanceDogFacts HAS
    `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that persistently occurs or continues to such a degree or extent that it unreasonably interferes with the peace, comfort or convenience of any person in any place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog is shown to be allowed to behave consistently in a manner contrary to the general interest of the community`                                                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed noise level measured by a prescribed method over a prescribed period of time`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed number of times of occurrence during or over a prescribed period of time`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38(1)
GIVEN f IS A NuisanceDogFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the dog is a nuisance` f MEANS
        f's `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that persistently occurs or continues to such a degree or extent that it unreasonably interferes with the peace, comfort or convenience of any person in any place`
    OR  f's `dog is shown to be allowed to behave consistently in a manner contrary to the general interest of the community`
    OR  f's `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed noise level measured by a prescribed method over a prescribed period of time`
    OR  f's `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed number of times of occurrence during or over a prescribed period of time`

-- s 38(2)-(3) -- a complaint lodged with an authorised person is the
-- trigger; if the authorised person is satisfied the dog is a nuisance as
-- alleged, the authorised person MAY (not must) issue an order. Modelled
-- as an eligibility/entitlement predicate for the authority to issue,
-- rather than a regulative rule, because the issuing decision is
-- discretionary and carries no deadline of its own -- the deadline
-- appears only once an order actually issues, in (3)'s "time specified in
-- the order" (encoded at s 38(5) below).
DECLARE NuisanceOrderApplication HAS
    `person lodged a complaint in the prescribed form with an authorised person, alleging that the dog is a nuisance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised person is satisfied that the dog is a nuisance as alleged in the complaint`                            IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38(2)-(3)
GIVEN app IS A NuisanceOrderApplication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the authorised person may issue a nuisance order under s 38(3)` app MEANS
        app's `person lodged a complaint in the prescribed form with an authorised person, alleging that the dog is a nuisance`
    AND app's `authorised person is satisfied that the dog is a nuisance as alleged in the complaint`

-- s 38(4) -- a nuisance order has effect for 6 months after the day it is
-- issued. Unit is MONTHS (not days) by this file's convention, since the
-- statute itself measures the period in months here (contrast s 34's
-- "reasonably necessary" test and the day-counted duties elsewhere in this
-- corpus).
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38(4)
GIVEN `months elapsed since the order was issued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the nuisance order remains in effect` `months elapsed since the order was issued` MEANS
    `months elapsed since the order was issued` AT MOST 6

-- s 38(5) -- the person to whom an order is issued must comply with it,
-- during the period it has effect, by the time specified in the order.
-- Genuine deadline-bearing duty -> regulative rule. The deadline itself is
-- not a fixed statutory number (it is whatever time the order specifies),
-- so it is a GIVEN parameter to the duty, measured in days by this file's
-- convention (matching the day-based WITHIN convention used elsewhere in
-- this corpus's dog-act-1976.l4).
DECLARE NuisanceDogParty IS ONE OF
    `Person To Whom The Nuisance Order Is Issued`
    -- corresponds, per s 38(3), to a "person liable for the control of the
    -- dog" (s 3, imported from dog-act-domain as LiableParty) -- but a
    -- DEONTIC's PARTY must be an enum tag, not a record, so the connection
    -- is documented here rather than typed directly.

DECLARE NuisanceDogAction IS ONE OF
    `prevent the behaviour that is alleged to constitute the nuisance`

@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38(3), (5)
GIVEN `time specified in the order, in days from the day it is issued, by which the behaviour must be prevented` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC NuisanceDogParty NuisanceDogAction
`s 38(5) compliance duty` `time specified in the order, in days from the day it is issued, by which the behaviour must be prevented` MEANS
    PARTY `Person To Whom The Nuisance Order Is Issued`
    MUST  `prevent the behaviour that is alleged to constitute the nuisance`
    WITHIN `time specified in the order, in days from the day it is issued, by which the behaviour must be prevented`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `Person To Whom The Nuisance Order Is Issued`
          BECAUSE "the person did not comply with the nuisance order by the time specified in it, as s 38(5) requires"

-- s 38(5) Penalty -- differs by whether the order relates to a dangerous
-- dog (s. 3, imported as DogProfile / `the dog is a dangerous dog`).
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38(5) Penalty
GIVEN dog IS A DogProfile
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 38(5) penalty` dog MEANS
    IF `the dog is a dangerous dog` dog
    THEN Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS JUST 500, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS JUST 500
    ELSE Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000,  `minimum fine` IS NOTHING,  `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

-- s 38(6) -- this section (the whole of s. 38, including the compliance
-- duty and its penalty) does not apply to a dog while it is kept at an
-- establishment licensed as an approved kennel establishment under s. 27
-- (outside this chunk's assigned range -- scoped out, fact-supplied).
@ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 38(6)
GIVEN `the dog is, at the relevant time, kept at an establishment licensed as an approved kennel establishment under s 27` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- @ref Dog Act 1976 (WA) s. 27 -- approved kennel establishment licensing, scoped out, fact-supplied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 38 applies to the dog` `the dog is, at the relevant time, kept at an establishment licensed as an approved kennel establishment under s 27` MEANS
    NOT `the dog is, at the relevant time, kept at an establishment licensed as an approved kennel establishment under s 27`

-- =============================================================================
-- Illustrations
-- =============================================================================

§ `Illustrations`

§§ `34(1) -- protection of an animal or bird`

`a lawful shooting to stop an attack` MEANS `S34(1) Facts` WITH
    `person owns, or is for the time being lawfully in charge of, the animal or bird` IS TRUE
    , `person found a dog attacking that animal or bird` IS TRUE
    , `there is no other way of stopping the attack` IS TRUE
    , `notice was given to a police officer as soon as is practicable after the shooting or destruction` IS TRUE

`a shooting with no notice given to police` MEANS `S34(1) Facts` WITH
    `person owns, or is for the time being lawfully in charge of, the animal or bird` IS TRUE
    , `person found a dog attacking that animal or bird` IS TRUE
    , `there is no other way of stopping the attack` IS TRUE
    , `notice was given to a police officer as soon as is practicable after the shooting or destruction` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `shooting or destroying a dog under s 34(1) is lawful` `a lawful shooting to stop an attack`
#ASSERT NOT (`shooting or destroying a dog under s 34(1) is lawful` `a shooting with no notice given to police`)

§§ `34(2) -- unaccompanied dog among confined livestock`

`a lawful destruction of an unaccompanied dog` MEANS `S34(2) Facts` WITH
    `person is the owner or occupier of the enclosed paddock, field, yard or other place confining the livestock, or is acting under that owner's or occupier's authority` IS TRUE
    , `the dog was found within that enclosed place` IS TRUE
    , `the dog was not accompanied by some person` IS TRUE

`a dog found accompanied by its handler` MEANS `S34(2) Facts` WITH
    `person is the owner or occupier of the enclosed paddock, field, yard or other place confining the livestock, or is acting under that owner's or occupier's authority` IS TRUE
    , `the dog was found within that enclosed place` IS TRUE
    , `the dog was not accompanied by some person` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `shooting or destroying a dog under s 34(2) is lawful` `a lawful destruction of an unaccompanied dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`shooting or destroying a dog under s 34(2) is lawful` `a dog found accompanied by its handler`)

§§ `34(3) -- evidentiary presumption`

#ASSERT `s 34(3) prima facie evidence that the person had the dog in possession or under control` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34(3) prima facie evidence that the person had the dog in possession or under control` FALSE)

§§ `34(4) -- poison-baiting`

`a compliant poison-baiting` MEANS PoisonLayingFacts WITH
    `laying of the poison was reasonably necessary for the protection of livestock confined or depasturing on the land` IS TRUE
    , `poison is not laid within 20 m of any road, reserve or public place` IS TRUE
    , `laying of the poison is authorised in the material circumstances by or under an Act relating to the prevention, destruction or eradication of specific kinds of animal or of animals in specified circumstances` IS TRUE
    , `poison is not laid so as to endanger children or indigenous birds or animals` IS TRUE

`a poison-baiting laid too close to a public road` MEANS PoisonLayingFacts WITH
    `laying of the poison was reasonably necessary for the protection of livestock confined or depasturing on the land` IS TRUE
    , `poison is not laid within 20 m of any road, reserve or public place` IS FALSE
    , `laying of the poison is authorised in the material circumstances by or under an Act relating to the prevention, destruction or eradication of specific kinds of animal or of animals in specified circumstances` IS TRUE
    , `poison is not laid so as to endanger children or indigenous birds or animals` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `laying poison under s 34(4) is lawful` `a compliant poison-baiting`
#ASSERT NOT (`laying poison under s 34(4) is lawful` `a poison-baiting laid too close to a public road`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34(4) offence -- laying poison in baits outside the lawful conditions` `a compliant poison-baiting`)
#ASSERT `s 34(4) offence -- laying poison in baits outside the lawful conditions` `a poison-baiting laid too close to a public road`
#ASSERT `s 34(4) penalty` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 1_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

§§ `35 -- immunity for lawful vermin/wandering-dog destruction measures`

`a compliant vermin-destruction measure` MEANS `S35 Facts` WITH
    `person reasonably and in good faith lawfully took measures for the purpose of destroying vermin or dogs wandering at large` IS TRUE
    , `measures were taken in conformity with the provisions of an Act or the regulations made under it` IS TRUE
    , `a dog wandering at large suffered death, injury or harm as a consequence of those measures` IS TRUE

`measures not taken in good faith` MEANS `S35 Facts` WITH
    `person reasonably and in good faith lawfully took measures for the purpose of destroying vermin or dogs wandering at large` IS FALSE
    , `measures were taken in conformity with the provisions of an Act or the regulations made under it` IS TRUE
    , `a dog wandering at large suffered death, injury or harm as a consequence of those measures` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `immunity from liability applies under s 35` `a compliant vermin-destruction measure`
#ASSERT NOT (`immunity from liability applies under s 35` `measures not taken in good faith`)

§§ `38(1) -- nuisance dogs`

`a persistently barking dog` MEANS NuisanceDogFacts WITH
    `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that persistently occurs or continues to such a degree or extent that it unreasonably interferes with the peace, comfort or convenience of any person in any place` IS TRUE
    , `dog is shown to be allowed to behave consistently in a manner contrary to the general interest of the community` IS FALSE
    , `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed noise level measured by a prescribed method over a prescribed period of time` IS FALSE
    , `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed number of times of occurrence during or over a prescribed period of time` IS FALSE

`a well-behaved dog with no complaint grounds` MEANS NuisanceDogFacts WITH
    `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that persistently occurs or continues to such a degree or extent that it unreasonably interferes with the peace, comfort or convenience of any person in any place` IS FALSE
    , `dog is shown to be allowed to behave consistently in a manner contrary to the general interest of the community` IS FALSE
    , `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed noise level measured by a prescribed method over a prescribed period of time` IS FALSE
    , `dog makes a noise, by barking or otherwise, that exceeds a prescribed number of times of occurrence during or over a prescribed period of time` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the dog is a nuisance` `a persistently barking dog`
#ASSERT NOT (`the dog is a nuisance` `a well-behaved dog with no complaint grounds`)

§§ `38(2)-(3) -- complaint and order-issuing authority`

`a complaint the authorised person is satisfied about` MEANS NuisanceOrderApplication WITH
    `person lodged a complaint in the prescribed form with an authorised person, alleging that the dog is a nuisance` IS TRUE
    , `authorised person is satisfied that the dog is a nuisance as alleged in the complaint` IS TRUE

`a complaint the authorised person is not satisfied about` MEANS NuisanceOrderApplication WITH
    `person lodged a complaint in the prescribed form with an authorised person, alleging that the dog is a nuisance` IS TRUE
    , `authorised person is satisfied that the dog is a nuisance as alleged in the complaint` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the authorised person may issue a nuisance order under s 38(3)` `a complaint the authorised person is satisfied about`
#ASSERT NOT (`the authorised person may issue a nuisance order under s 38(3)` `a complaint the authorised person is not satisfied about`)

§§ `38(4) -- 6-month duration`

#ASSERT `the nuisance order remains in effect` 3
#ASSERT `the nuisance order remains in effect` 6
#ASSERT NOT (`the nuisance order remains in effect` 7)

§§ `38(5) -- compliance duty and penalty`

#TRACE `s 38(5) compliance duty` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Person To Whom The Nuisance Order Is Issued` DOES `prevent the behaviour that is alleged to constitute the nuisance` AT 10
-- Result: FULFILLED (the behaviour was prevented within the 14-day window specified in the order)

#TRACE `s 38(5) compliance duty` 14 AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 15)
-- Result: DEONTIC BREACHED -- the behaviour was not prevented within the time specified in the order

`a nuisance order relating to a dangerous dog` MEANS `a declared dangerous dog`
`a nuisance order relating to an ordinary dog` MEANS `a non-dangerous dog`

`a non-dangerous dog` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS FALSE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS FALSE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

`a declared dangerous dog` MEANS DogProfile WITH
    `declared to be a dangerous dog (declared) under s 33E(1)` IS TRUE
    , `is a dangerous dog (restricted breed)` IS FALSE
    , `is a commercial security dog` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 38(5) penalty` `a nuisance order relating to a dangerous dog` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 10_000, `minimum fine` IS JUST 500, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS JUST 500
#ASSERT `s 38(5) penalty` `a nuisance order relating to an ordinary dog` EQUALS Penalty WITH fine IS JUST 5_000, `minimum fine` IS NOTHING, `imprisonment months` IS NOTHING, `further offence fine` IS NOTHING

§§ `38(6) -- approved kennel establishment exemption`

#ASSERT `s 38 applies to the dog` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 38 applies to the dog` TRUE)
